title Incense, index-row red on the open 20261010 shelf confirmed, booking held by ledger bound
prompt Baton lap for the incense seat: read the inner prompt and the card, round-open, claim-as-override if the lane queue is empty, and land whatever is honest.
think The card's agent-doable queue reads parked: %642 waits on a scrub trade, %519 is ordinary touch-on work, and the third item waits on Keaton's word. Every incense queue entry needs a word, so nothing in this lane is mine to build alone.
think Pheromone's session log of 20261010.123039 named an index-row red on the open shelf 20261010. I did not take that reading on trust: I ran the witness myself, tools/in/index_row_bound_witness.rish, and it failed on that shelf.
think The same class is already booked for the 20261009 shelf as REDS %835. The 20261010 shelf is a recurrence, and no row for it stands on the fetched ledger.
think The anointed spine derives the next free number as %840 from xy/main, so the booking is ready to write except for one fact: construction/REDS.md reads 65527 of its 65536-byte bound, nine bytes of headroom. A new row would refuse every commit on every ship.
think Booking the row needs a closed row folded off the pin first. That fold is a separate act, so I held the booking rather than widen this lap into a ledger reshuffle.
obs The red is real and reproduced on this tree. The booking is not done, and this log is the durable record until a fold makes room for it.
obs Repairing the shelf is not this lane's to do. Eight ships append to that file, and the witness counts peers' lines, so a repair here races the fleet.
obs The model field names the resolved runtime model from the local settings file. That is configuration evidence, not verified active telemetry, so model_status stays unverified.
loom witness=index_row_bound_witness verdict=rows_over_bound scope=open_shelf_20261010
rota none -- the finding came from the index witness and the baton's claim-as-override clause; no council row deep read this lap
orbit round 14 Earth -- what must stop: the booking waits behind the ledger's own bound, and the lap does not force a fold to make room
file construction/REDS.md the ledger read at 65527 of 65536 bytes; the next row %840 waits behind a fold of a closed row
file session-logs/date/README-index-20261010.md the open shelf the index witness reads red; this log adds one row beneath the delimiter and repairs nothing
file recursion-prompts/incense-inner.md the inner prompt read; its state and next did not move this lap
scope incense lane, hold with a finding; no code, witness, ledger row, or peer row touched
status HOLD with a finding -- index_row_bound_witness reads verdict=rows_over_bound on the open shelf 20261010; REDS %840 derived from xy/main but unbooked because construction/REDS.md is 9 bytes under its bound
recommend check in (either) -- Keaton's word on which closed row folds off the ledger pin so %840 can book, or a shelf-owning seat to repair the 20261010 index lines
